# `pnpm dev` and running the web tier directly: copy to apps/web/.env. Never
# commit real values. Compose sets this tier's variables itself and reads no
# `.env` into it.
#
# This tier holds no credentials. It proxies `/api/*` to the API process and
# renders. DATABASE_URL, the GitHub App private key, the webhook secret, the
# OAuth client secret and SESSION_KEY_V1 belong in `apps/api/.env`, and putting
# them here loads them into the process that terminates public traffic for no
# functional gain. Every variable: docs/self-host/configuration.md

# Where `/api/*` is proxied. Leave unset to use the API's loopback default,
# which is what `pnpm dev` starts.
# MERGEBRIEF_API_ORIGIN=http://127.0.0.1:3001

# Public origin (scheme + host, no trailing slash). `pnpm start` reads it from
# here and serves its hostname.
# `vite dev` does not: its host guard reads the shell before this file loads, so
# for a tunnel run `export PUBLIC_BASE_URL=https://<subdomain>.ngrok-free.app`
# (docs/dev/webhook-loop.md).
# The API refuses a signed-in browser's state-changing request from any other
# origin, so browse the app at exactly the API's PUBLIC_BASE_URL.
PUBLIC_BASE_URL=http://localhost:3000

# Where `pnpm start` listens. `vite dev` ignores both and serves on 3000.
# MERGEBRIEF_WEB_HOST=0.0.0.0
# MERGEBRIEF_WEB_PORT=3000

# error | warn | info | debug. Default: info.
# LOG_LEVEL=info

# Feature flags, read when the web bundle is built, so they have no effect on a
# pulled image. Everything matching ENABLE_* is inlined into the client bundle:
# boolean toggles only, never a secret. `true` or `1` shows the language picker;
# the catalog and locale machinery stay wired either way.
# ENABLE_LANGUAGE_SELECTION=true
